' status: implemented contracts; PLANNED acceptance remains for the open live gates below.
' Primary reports focused source/unit and persisted offline native fixture passes.
' Security/adversarial repairs are implemented; their re-evaluations remain in progress.
' Approval update: the Executor explicitly requested automatic permissions (YOLO)
' for proveo run opencode; this supersedes the former human shell-checkpoint policy.
' Preserved crew and auth boundary: _spec/defs/opencode/opencode-paradigm.puml
' Crew module layout: _spec/defs/opencode/opencode-topology.puml
' Shipped package pin: _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml
' Shared hook semantics: _spec/packages/lib/git-sync-turn.puml
' Host-side launch timing: _spec/internal/sbx/launch-env.puml
' Mobile transport ownership: _spec/internal/sbx/host-android-adb.puml
' Persistence transport: _spec/packages/lib/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml
'
' Implemented native contract, inspected in source and backed by focused fixture tests:
' agents replaces agent; permissions is an ordered action/resource/effect list.
' update: disable replaces autoupdate; compaction.auto: true replaces context flags.
' Default seeds select no model, including no title model or agent model.
' Generated YAML removes the old temperature key before native permission decoding.
' Both local-provider writers use providers.ollama.package and settings, with
' package @opencode/ai/providers/openai-compatible and the existing /v1 endpoint.
' An explicit local-model request selects root model and agents.title.model, not small_model.
' OpenCode mobile MCP uses mcp.servers.mobile and disabled: false, not enabled: true.
' The plugin default-exports an object with id and setup(ctx); its observer uses
' the context event stream and event.data for session.idle through ctx.event.subscribe.
' Focused plugin/runtime contracts do not establish model-driven live idle completion.
' Do not revive the v1 named export or returned event callback.
' Authentication comes from launch environment credentials or broker sentinels;
' in-sandbox login is not the supported authentication path.
'
' Permission migration is mechanical, not an opportunity to tighten delegation:
' preserve ordering and existing effects for edit and native shell actions.
' plan: edit deny, shell deny. build: edit allow, shell ask.
' Those are native role rules, not a claim that each ask needs a human response.
' session.permissions: autoaccept accepts ask requests; explicit denies retain
' native semantics. Risky-operation house rules remain prompt instructions,
' not an interactive native approval gate. Do not add new delegation restrictions.
' Runtime native_command injects --auto once for headless run, independently of
' evidence verbosity. No other native command gains this run-specific approval flag.
' The persisted offline fixture executes the actual native shell tool: ask runs,
' explicit deny returns Permission denied: shell, and direct run without --auto
' rejects a non-interactive ask. These are native simulator tests, not live model tests.
' Advisors: edit deny, shell deny. spec-keeper: edit allow, shell deny; its
' existing prompt limits editing to _spec/, PLAN.md, and AGENTS.md.
' Do not introduce path-filter enforcement or new delegation denies by default.
' Config, generated user agent files, and project AGENTS.md remain missing-only;
' OPENCODE_RESEED=1 is the existing explicit replacement override.
' Explicit local-model/add-on wiring remains distinct from default reseeding.
' Shared proveo_bootstrap_opencode_config replaces the old sample-search fallback.
' Restore config, seed missing defaults, render agents, wire config, then release;
' preserve user JSON/JSONC and existing generated agents unless explicit reseed.
' Retain $schema: https://opencode.ai/config.json as the documented editor pointer.
' Its published root schema still describes v1; validate native contracts with the
' pinned binary rather than replacing correct v2 fields to satisfy that schema.
'
' Native CLI config documentation: https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/cli/config
' General editor schema pointer: https://opencode.ai/config.json (v1; advisory).
' Native schema/behavior evidence: e2e/testdata/opencode_presentation.py,
' e2e/testdata/opencode_presentation.mjs, and their persisted JSON fixture.
' Exact OPENCODE_CLI_CONFIG_CONTENT payload quoted from the image and fixture:
' {
'   "session": {
'     "permissions": "autoaccept", "markdown": "source", "thinking": "show",
'     "grouping": "none", "verbosity": "high", "sidebar": "auto"
'   },
'   "tabs": {"mode": "on", "indicators": "status"},
'   "mini": {
'     "tools": "show", "thinking": "show", "shell_output": "show",
'     "turn_summary": "show", "footer": "show"
'   }
' }
' Inline preferences override saved global cli.json without modifying that file.
' Source Markdown disables concealment; thinking show expands full returned blocks.
' High verbosity and grouping none expose individual calls/thoughts, not grouped summaries.
' The eight session/tab values are observed in the actual native TUI Settings dialog.
' Each of the five mini fields has a native invalid-value schema control; this does
' not claim that live model-driven mini output was exercised by the offline fixture.
' Child transcript navigation and the unsupported main-transcript wait-graph default
' are documented by the owning crew diagram and primary's native UI/source audit.
'
' The Executor chose a private per-run database and a full-lifetime durable-store lease.
' Stateful runs sharing that store must serialize through the full writer lifetime,
' including descendants and publication; failure must preserve recoverable session data.
' proveo-seed must scrub durable/legacy stores with runtime --sanitize (brief lease) and
' release before the long seed body: sbx starts the agent concurrently with durable
' startup, so wrapping seed in --preflight-command held the lease past await-seed's
' 30s launch-anyway window and the agent exited 75 ("another OpenCode run owns…").
' Focused lifecycle fixtures exercise these boundaries; final review is still pending.
' v2 stores auth tokens in SQLite alongside durable session state.
' Removing auth.json alone is insufficient; deleting the session database is forbidden.
' Cover every native account token store, provider credentials, and mcp-auth stores;
' an empty credential table alone is not proof of credential-free persistence.
' Implemented token handling covers credential, account, control_account, account_state,
' auth.json, and mcp-auth.json. Schema-specific sanitization applies only to native
' databases at the data root; ordinary Git/reference SQLite files copy unchanged.
' Preserve session/history/resume data and safely exclude or scrub credentials on
' every persistence path, including database journals, snapshots, and restored state.
' Preserve nonauth state and artifacts rather than dropping the entire data directory.
' Session and artifact paths must resolve after restore across backend mappings;
' durable history must not depend on a deleted private runtime directory.
' Non-auth native state persists; artifact output and stored session paths rebase to
' the canonical durable store instead of retaining the per-run temporary prefix.
' The wrapper uses manifest/config mappings for the same Docker and sbx store;
' divergent legacy/canonical histories fail rather than silently overwriting either.
' Protected orphan recovery retains source/lease records on publication failure;
' controlling-PTY suspend/resume and descendant lifetime ownership have source fixtures.
' Do not infer cross-VM filesystem lock behavior from local fixture serialization.
' Do not silently broaden PROVEO_KEEP_AGENT_LOGINS to allow persisted v2 tokens.
'
' Verification scope reported by primary, not commands executed by spec-keeper:
' - all five diagrams passed per-file PlantUML checks and the enforced note-box test
'   before this revision; edited diagrams require the normal post-edit recheck.
' - focused source/unit suites passed, including repaired credential/runtime fixtures.
' - persisted offline native presentation/shell-policy fixtures passed against v2.0.25.
' Current execution evidence: rebuilt proveo/opencode:local resolves @opencode/cli@2.0.26.
' Targeted Docker e2e gates cover snapshots, native lifecycle, presentation, seeded registry,
' and two actual proveo runs; the native simulator also checks first-session transcript resume.
' Remaining acceptance: adversarial/security re-evaluations and the full image/e2e suites.
' Actual sbx cross-VM file locking and model-driven
' live idle git synchronization remain unexecuted because sbx/tooling is unavailable.
' The offline simulator scripts the model stream; it does not establish live provider,
' child-operation rendering, or network-backed idle commit/push behavior.
' Image-backed native fixtures derive their expected version from proveo.agent.version.
' They require a v2 pin and compare the native version exactly, without a fixed fixture release.
' The two-run regression creates separate native CLI sessions and resumes the first after both exits.
' It checks both root IDs and transcripts, including that the second transcript remains unchanged.
' e2e/opencode_sessions_test.go launches separate actual proveo run opencode Docker containers.
' Both ended session IDs must appear through --ls and remain retrievable after container teardown.
' The registry probe loads /api/config before listing agents on the same private native server.
' A fresh agent-only diagnostic can return the uninitialized empty registry before configuration loads.
' Runtime database publication is distinct from git synchronization: never turn idle
' commit/push into an awaited CLI-return gate or promise completion after CLI exit.
'
' Register: manual normalized word/syllable counts; two sentences per note.
' FK: note bottom of DEFAULTS; words=30 syllables=55; FK 11.9
' FK: note bottom of FM; words=28 syllables=53; FK 12.2
' FK: note bottom of GO; words=27 syllables=52; FK 12.4
' FK: note bottom of HOME; words=30 syllables=51; FK 10.3
' FK: note bottom of PLUGIN; words=33 syllables=61; FK 12.7
' FK: note bottom of TESTS; words=33 syllables=60; FK 12.3
' FK: note bottom of POLICY; words=32 syllables=57; FK 11.7
' FK: note bottom of RUNTIME; words=34 syllables=59; FK 11.5
' FK: note bottom of CREDENTIALS; words=32 syllables=59; FK 12.4
' FK: note bottom of STATE; words=31 syllables=57; FK 12.2
' FK: note bottom of PREFS; words=34 syllables=63; FK 12.9
' FK: note bottom of CLI; words=32 syllables=56; FK 11.3
' FK: note bottom of CREDENTIALS (native scope); words=34 syllables=61; FK 12.2

!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Native OpenCode v2 integration — implemented; PLANNED live acceptance
left to right direction

package "defs/opencode" {
  component "defaults/opencode.json\nsample_opencode.json" as DEFAULTS <<app>>
  component "entrypoint.sh\nseed + local-provider writer" as EP <<app>>
  component "Dockerfile\n@opencode/cli pin\nOPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=1" as IMAGE <<host>>
  component "opencode.json\nagents + ordered permissions\nupdate: disable · compaction.auto: true\nno default model selection" as CONFIG <<app>>
}

component "defs/subagents/_frontmatter/opencode\nnative permissions; no old temperature key" as FM <<app>>
component "packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh\nrender_subagents · seed · persistence" as LIB <<app>>
component "opencode session\nsession.permissions: autoaccept\nexplicit denies remain denied" as POLICY <<app>>
component "OPENCODE_CLI_CONFIG_CONTENT\nnative session/tabs/mini preferences\noverrides global cli.json without rewriting it" as PREFS <<app>>
component "internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go\nlaunchConfigEnv\nOPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT" as GO <<app>>
component "internal/hostadb/hostadb.go\nmcp.servers.mobile\ndisabled: false" as ADB <<app>>
component "opencode\nroot logger: --log-level debug\nheadless run: --auto independent of evidence\nverbose run: --thinking --print-logs\nroot TUI: no stderr log streaming" as CLI <<app>>
component "packages/lib/hooks/proveo-git-sync-turn.js\ndefault {id, setup(ctx)}\nctx.event.subscribe · event.data" as PLUGIN <<async>>
component "packages/lib/hooks/git-sync-turn.sh\nbest-effort idle dialect\nsubject helper: opencode run --standalone" as HOOK <<app>>
component "internal/proveohome\nsession-preserving credential boundary" as HOME <<app>>
component "packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime\nprivate per-run DB\nfull-lifetime durable-store lease" as RUNTIME <<app>>
component "packages/lib/opencode-credentials.py\nnative provider/account/MCP token removal\nordinary reference SQLite unchanged" as CREDENTIALS <<app>>
database "OpenCode durable state\nsessions + nonauth state + artifacts\nrestorable backend paths" as STATE <<db>>
component "internal/contract\ninternal/imagetest/opencode_test.go\ne2e" as TESTS <<app>>

DEFAULTS ARROW_MAIN EP : missing-only; explicit reseed
EP ARROW_MAIN CONFIG : native defaults + requested local model
FM ARROW_MAIN LIB : render native agent YAML
LIB ARROW_MAIN CONFIG : preserve user files
ADB ARROW_MAIN GO : requested mobile server
GO ARROW_MAIN CLI : one composed native inline config
CONFIG ARROW_MAIN CLI : persistent user configuration
IMAGE ARROW_MAIN CLI : pinned CLI; updater disabled
IMAGE ARROW_MAIN PREFS : exact inline native CLI preferences
PREFS ARROW_MAIN POLICY : session.permissions: autoaccept
PREFS ARROW_MAIN CLI : presentation defaults; global preferences preserved
CONFIG ARROW_MAIN POLICY : role rules remain native
POLICY ARROW_MAIN CLI : automatic asks, not per-shell HITL
LIB ARROW_MAIN PLUGIN : install before plugin loading
CLI ARROW_QUEUE PLUGIN : idle notification, not a return gate
PLUGIN ARROW_QUEUE HOOK : start best-effort helper; stdin closed
RUNTIME ARROW_MAIN CLI : private active database
RUNTIME ARROW_MAIN CLI : headless run --auto exactly once
RUNTIME ARROW_MAIN STATE : exclusive lifecycle ownership
RUNTIME ARROW_MAIN CREDENTIALS : credential-free persistence boundary
CREDENTIALS ARROW_MAIN STATE : preserve resumable state and artifacts
HOME ARROW_MAIN RUNTIME : backend durable-store mapping
LIB ARROW_MAIN HOME : restore/save must preserve the invariant
TESTS ARROW_OPTIONAL CONFIG : native decoding and effective permissions
TESTS ARROW_OPTIONAL CLI : image + live acceptance
TESTS ARROW_OPTIONAL HOME : sessions retained; credentials absent
TESTS ARROW_OPTIONAL HOOK : eventual completion; no return gate
TESTS ARROW_OPTIONAL POLICY : automatic asks; native deny semantics
TESTS ARROW_OPTIONAL PREFS : native TUI eight values; mini schema controls

note bottom of DEFAULTS
  Seed only missing files so user config
  remains under user control. An explicit reseed
  may replace those defaults, but this migration
  preserves permission rules without adding
  new restrictions on delegation.
end note

note bottom of FM
  Remove the old ""temperature"" key from
  generated agent YAML. Its presence selects the
  legacy decoder, which can silently discard
  native permissions even when the file
  otherwise looks valid.
end note

note bottom of GO
  Both provider writers must emit the same
  native config before launch. The inline
  payload combines local-model and mobile-server
  settings so one environment entry cannot
  overwrite the other.
end note

note bottom of HOME
  Keep session history when scrubbing stored
  credentials from storage. The safe lifecycle
  must leave durable state free of tokens and
  keys across every persistence path, not erase
  the session database.
end note

note bottom of PLUGIN
  The idle observer provides best-effort git sync
  after a completed turn. It must start the git
  helper without making CLI return depend on
  that helper finishing, so eventual completion
  remains the only guarantee.
end note

note bottom of TESTS
  Static tests must inspect decoded native
  permissions, not just matching text. Image and
  live tests must verify preserved user files,
  resumable sessions, credential-free state, and
  eventual idle git sync against the pinned CLI.
end note

note bottom of POLICY
  Automatic session approval satisfies ask rules
  without requiring a human checkpoint for each
  shell command. Explicit deny rules keep their
  native meaning, while risk guidance remains
  an instruction, not an approval gate.
end note

note bottom of RUNTIME
  Each stateful run uses a private database while
  holding a full-lifetime lease on its durable
  store. The lease must prevent concurrent
  publication and preserve recoverable session
  state when a run fails or is interrupted.
end note

note bottom of CREDENTIALS
  Scrub every native account token store as well
  as provider credentials and MCP auth. A clean
  credential table alone cannot make durable
  state safe when another account store still
  retains authentication tokens.
end note

note bottom of STATE
  Preserve nonauth state and artifacts when moving
  sessions between backend storage layouts.
  Session paths must resolve after restore, rather
  than retaining a private runtime directory that
  disappears when the process exits.
end note

note bottom of PREFS
  Inline CLI preferences win over saved global
  choices without rewriting the user's file.
  The image can expose execution and accept ask
  requests while preserving durable settings for
  runs that do not inherit this environment.
end note

note bottom of CLI
  Headless automatic approval comes from the
  runtime flag rather than the evidence switches.
  Add that flag once so ask requests can execute
  without narration, while explicit deny rules
  still reject the operation.
end note

note bottom of CREDENTIALS
  Only native databases at the data root undergo
  token scrubbing, so ordinary Git databases stay
  intact. Apply the native auth schema only to
  those stores, not every file that uses the
  same database format.
end note
@enduml
